{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FWsPdgCyzR8uvTi73mN6bd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# KERTAS TUGASAN / ASSIGNMENT SHEET\n2\t\n3\t**Kod WIM / WIM Code:** G452-010-3:2023-C05/KT(1/4)\n4\t**Kertas Warna / Paper Color:** MERAH JAMBU / PINK\n5\t\n6\t## Work Activity 1: Conduct BEV Daily Briefing | **Reference:** C05/KP(1/4)\n7\t\n8\t### S1 — Short Answer: List SIX (6) items that should be covered in a BEV workshop daily briefing.\n9\t### S2 — MCQ: What is the recommended maximum duration for a daily briefing? A. 5 minutes B. 15-20 minutes C. 45 minutes D. 1 hour\n10\t### S3 — T/F: a) Attendance list is optional for daily briefings. b) The job control board should be updated after the briefing. c) Safety concerns raised during briefing should be documented.\n11\t### S4 — Short Answer: Explain THREE (3) effective communication techniques for conducting a daily briefing.\n12\t### S5 — Short Answer: Describe the role of the job control board in workshop management. What information should it display?\n13\t\n14\t## Skema Jawapan\n15\t**S1:** Safety reminder, work progress update, new assignments, service information updates, housekeeping/5S, questions and feedback.\n16\t**S2:** B\n17\t**S3:** a) FALSE — mandatory, auditable document b) TRUE c) TRUE\n18\t**S4:** Clarity (simple/direct language), brevity (concise), structure (consistent format), engagement (questions/input), visual aids (whiteboard/job board). Any three.\n19\t**S5:** Displays: vehicle registration and job status, technician assignments, expected completion times, parts status. Updated daily to track workshop workflow.\n20\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"34b7e541-fc46-443f-9329-800f1caa525b","uuid":"0cfa12a6-0c0f-4392-958e-c3797d291fa2","timestamp":"2026-04-16T16:18:16.951Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\bev-diagnostic-rectification\\C05\\KT-01.md","content":"# KERTAS TUGASAN / ASSIGNMENT SHEET\n\n**Kod WIM / WIM Code:** G452-010-3:2023-C05/KT(1/4)\n**Kertas Warna / Paper Color:** MERAH JAMBU / PINK\n\n## Work Activity 1: Conduct BEV Daily Briefing | **Reference:** C05/KP(1/4)\n\n### S1 — Short Answer: List SIX (6) items that should be covered in a BEV workshop daily briefing.\n### S2 — MCQ: What is the recommended maximum duration for a daily briefing? A. 5 minutes B. 15-20 minutes C. 45 minutes D. 1 hour\n### S3 — T/F: a) Attendance list is optional for daily briefings. b) The job control board should be updated after the briefing. c) Safety concerns raised during briefing should be documented.\n### S4 — Short Answer: Explain THREE (3) effective communication techniques for conducting a daily briefing.\n### S5 — Short Answer: Describe the role of the job control board in workshop management. What information should it display?\n\n## Skema Jawapan\n**S1:** Safety reminder, work progress update, new assignments, service information updates, housekeeping/5S, questions and feedback.\n**S2:** B\n**S3:** a) FALSE — mandatory, auditable document b) TRUE c) TRUE\n**S4:** Clarity (simple/direct language), brevity (concise), structure (consistent format), engagement (questions/input), visual aids (whiteboard/job board). Any three.\n**S5:** Displays: vehicle registration and job status, technician assignments, expected completion times, parts status. Updated daily to track workshop workflow.\n","numLines":20,"startLine":1,"totalLines":20}}}
