{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019DgDkEaGaj9deGhZx1kMWK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# KERTAS TUGASAN / ASSIGNMENT SHEET\n2\t\n3\t**Kod WIM / WIM Code:** G452-010-3:2023-C05/KT(2/4)\n4\t**Kertas Warna / Paper Color:** MERAH JAMBU / PINK\n5\t\n6\t## Work Activity 2: Monitor BEV Subordinate's Performance | **Reference:** C05/KP(2/4)\n7\t\n8\t### S1 — Short Answer: List FOUR (4) evaluation dimensions used to assess BEV technician performance.\n9\t### S2 — MCQ: Which is a performance improvement technique for skill gaps? A. Salary increase B. On-the-Job Training (OJT) C. Vacation D. Transfer\n10\t### S3 — Matching: 1. Evaluation form 2. Counselling form 3. Training nomination form (a. Recommend training for skill gaps b. Document counselling sessions c. Formal performance rating)\n11\t### S4 — Short Answer: Describe TWO (2) BEV-specific competency indicators a supervisor should assess.\n12\t### S5 — T/F: a) Performance appraisal is only done annually. b) Counselling is used for persistent performance problems. c) Performance reports are confidential documents.\n13\t### S6 — Short Answer: What FOUR (4) improvement techniques can a supervisor use for underperforming technicians?\n14\t\n15\t## Skema Jawapan\n16\t**S1:** Attitude, skills, knowledge, productivity and efficiency.\n17\t**S2:** B\n18\t**S3:** 1-c, 2-b, 3-a\n19\t**S4:** Can technician independently perform HV de-energisation? Do they consistently follow safety procedures? Can they interpret BEV diagnostic fault codes? Any two.\n20\t**S5:** a) FALSE — formal annually/semi-annually, informal monthly b) TRUE c) TRUE\n21\t**S6:** On-the-Job Training (OJT), refresher course, counselling, mentoring.\n22\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"34b7e541-fc46-443f-9329-800f1caa525b","uuid":"deb8f59e-d392-4762-aee6-124bcd219ad2","timestamp":"2026-04-16T16:18:17.240Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\bev-diagnostic-rectification\\C05\\KT-02.md","content":"# KERTAS TUGASAN / ASSIGNMENT SHEET\n\n**Kod WIM / WIM Code:** G452-010-3:2023-C05/KT(2/4)\n**Kertas Warna / Paper Color:** MERAH JAMBU / PINK\n\n## Work Activity 2: Monitor BEV Subordinate's Performance | **Reference:** C05/KP(2/4)\n\n### S1 — Short Answer: List FOUR (4) evaluation dimensions used to assess BEV technician performance.\n### S2 — MCQ: Which is a performance improvement technique for skill gaps? A. Salary increase B. On-the-Job Training (OJT) C. Vacation D. Transfer\n### S3 — Matching: 1. Evaluation form 2. Counselling form 3. Training nomination form (a. Recommend training for skill gaps b. Document counselling sessions c. Formal performance rating)\n### S4 — Short Answer: Describe TWO (2) BEV-specific competency indicators a supervisor should assess.\n### S5 — T/F: a) Performance appraisal is only done annually. b) Counselling is used for persistent performance problems. c) Performance reports are confidential documents.\n### S6 — Short Answer: What FOUR (4) improvement techniques can a supervisor use for underperforming technicians?\n\n## Skema Jawapan\n**S1:** Attitude, skills, knowledge, productivity and efficiency.\n**S2:** B\n**S3:** 1-c, 2-b, 3-a\n**S4:** Can technician independently perform HV de-energisation? Do they consistently follow safety procedures? Can they interpret BEV diagnostic fault codes? Any two.\n**S5:** a) FALSE — formal annually/semi-annually, informal monthly b) TRUE c) TRUE\n**S6:** On-the-Job Training (OJT), refresher course, counselling, mentoring.\n","numLines":22,"startLine":1,"totalLines":22}}}
