{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TfiBhprigXDoAUHD8yDrQM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# KERTAS TUGASAN / ASSIGNMENT SHEET\n2\t\n3\t**Kod WIM / WIM Code:** G452-010-3:2023-C05/KT(4/4)\n4\t**Kertas Warna / Paper Color:** MERAH JAMBU / PINK\n5\t\n6\t## Work Activity 4: Monitor BEV Workshop Safety, Health & Environment | **Reference:** C05/KP(4/4)\n7\t\n8\t### S1 — Short Answer: List FOUR (4) employer responsibilities and FOUR (4) employee responsibilities under OSHA 1994 relevant to a BEV workshop.\n9\t### S2 — MCQ: Which emergency response is specific to BEV workshops? A. Fire drill B. Earthquake drill C. Electric shock response using rescue hook and AED D. Flood evacuation\n10\t### S3 — Short Answer: List FIVE (5) \"Do's\" and FIVE (5) \"Don'ts\" for BEV workshop safety.\n11\t### S4 — Short Answer: Describe the format and contents of a SHE finding report. Include at least SIX (6) sections.\n12\t### S5 — T/F: a) Fire extinguisher checks are done annually only. b) Near-miss reports are optional. c) The supervisor should conduct daily hazard walk-throughs.\n13\t### S6 — Short Answer: Explain the risk assessment process for a SHE finding. Include severity, likelihood, and risk rating.\n14\t\n15\t## Skema Jawapan\n16\t**S1:** Employer: provide safe workplace, train/certify staff, maintain safety equipment, provide PPE. Employee: follow safety procedures, wear PPE, report hazards, participate in training.\n17\t**S2:** C\n18\t**S3:** Do's: de-energise HV, verify zero energy, wear PPE, use insulated tools, maintain two-person rule. Don'ts: assume HV disconnected, wear jewellery, skip discharge waiting, use damaged PPE, work alone on HV.\n19\t**S4:** Date/time, location, finding description, photo evidence, risk assessment, recommendation, responsible person, target date, follow-up.\n20\t**S5:** a) FALSE — monthly or per company schedule b) FALSE — mandatory to report c) TRUE\n21\t**S6:** Severity (minor to critical), likelihood (unlikely to almost certain), risk rating (low to extreme) = severity x likelihood. Photo, date, recommendation included.\n22\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"34b7e541-fc46-443f-9329-800f1caa525b","uuid":"675ff119-1c63-478d-8771-b3bff677f779","timestamp":"2026-04-16T16:18:21.899Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\bev-diagnostic-rectification\\C05\\KT-04.md","content":"# KERTAS TUGASAN / ASSIGNMENT SHEET\n\n**Kod WIM / WIM Code:** G452-010-3:2023-C05/KT(4/4)\n**Kertas Warna / Paper Color:** MERAH JAMBU / PINK\n\n## Work Activity 4: Monitor BEV Workshop Safety, Health & Environment | **Reference:** C05/KP(4/4)\n\n### S1 — Short Answer: List FOUR (4) employer responsibilities and FOUR (4) employee responsibilities under OSHA 1994 relevant to a BEV workshop.\n### S2 — MCQ: Which emergency response is specific to BEV workshops? A. Fire drill B. Earthquake drill C. Electric shock response using rescue hook and AED D. Flood evacuation\n### S3 — Short Answer: List FIVE (5) \"Do's\" and FIVE (5) \"Don'ts\" for BEV workshop safety.\n### S4 — Short Answer: Describe the format and contents of a SHE finding report. Include at least SIX (6) sections.\n### S5 — T/F: a) Fire extinguisher checks are done annually only. b) Near-miss reports are optional. c) The supervisor should conduct daily hazard walk-throughs.\n### S6 — Short Answer: Explain the risk assessment process for a SHE finding. Include severity, likelihood, and risk rating.\n\n## Skema Jawapan\n**S1:** Employer: provide safe workplace, train/certify staff, maintain safety equipment, provide PPE. Employee: follow safety procedures, wear PPE, report hazards, participate in training.\n**S2:** C\n**S3:** Do's: de-energise HV, verify zero energy, wear PPE, use insulated tools, maintain two-person rule. Don'ts: assume HV disconnected, wear jewellery, skip discharge waiting, use damaged PPE, work alone on HV.\n**S4:** Date/time, location, finding description, photo evidence, risk assessment, recommendation, responsible person, target date, follow-up.\n**S5:** a) FALSE — monthly or per company schedule b) FALSE — mandatory to report c) TRUE\n**S6:** Severity (minor to critical), likelihood (unlikely to almost certain), risk rating (low to extreme) = severity x likelihood. Photo, date, recommendation included.\n","numLines":22,"startLine":1,"totalLines":22}}}
