{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LvyogM4thYHBJs9QmL4EE2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# KERTAS KERJA / WORK SHEET\n2\t\n3\t**Kod WIM / WIM Code:** G452-010-3:2023-C05/KK(1/4)\n4\t**Kertas Warna / Paper Color:** BIRU / BLUE\n5\t\n6\t## Work Activity 1: Conduct BEV Daily Briefing\n7\t\n8\t## Objektif Prestasi\n9\t1. Prepare daily briefing information and assignments\n10\t2. Execute a daily briefing session\n11\t3. Record daily briefing feedback and update the job control board\n12\t\n13\t## Materials\n14\t- Briefing agenda template, attendance list form, job control board (whiteboard), sample work orders/job cards, marker pens\n15\t\n16\t## Prosedur Kerja\n17\t\n18\t### Step 1: Prepare Briefing\n19\t1.1 Review previous day's job status on job control board\n20\t1.2 Identify new vehicles received / scheduled for today\n21\t1.3 Allocate tasks to technicians based on skill level and workload\n22\t1.4 Prepare safety topic of the day\n23\t1.5 Gather any service information updates (TSBs, recalls)\n24\t1.6 Write briefing agenda\n25\t\n26\t### Step 2: Execute Briefing\n27\t2.1 Gather all technicians at briefing area\n28\t2.2 Circulate attendance list — all sign\n29\t2.3 Deliver briefing following prepared agenda:\n30\t   - Safety reminder (HV safety topic)\n31\t   - Work progress update from yesterday\n32\t   - New assignments — distribute job cards\n33\t   - Service information updates\n34\t   - Housekeeping / 5S compliance\n35\t2.4 Invite questions and feedback\n36\t2.5 Address concerns raised\n37\t2.6 Close briefing — team disperses to assignments\n38\t\n39\t### Step 3: Post-Briefing Actions\n40\t3.1 Update job control board with today's assignments\n41\t3.2 File attendance list and briefing notes\n42\t3.3 Document any safety concerns raised — initiate follow-up action\n43\t3.4 Monitor work progress during the day\n44\t\n45\t## Assessment Checklist\n46\t| Criteria | C | NYC |\n47\t|----------|---|-----|\n48\t| Briefing prepared with agenda covering all required items | [ ] | [ ] |\n49\t| Briefing delivered clearly within 15-20 minutes | [ ] | [ ] |\n50\t| Attendance list circulated and signed | [ ] | [ ] |\n51\t| Job allocation matched to technician skill level | [ ] | [ ] |\n52\t| Questions handled and feedback recorded | [ ] | [ ] |\n53\t| Job control board updated | [ ] | [ ] |\n54\t| Clear, confident communication demonstrated | [ ] | [ ] |\n55\t\n56\t**Trainee:** _______________ **Instructor:** _______________ **Date:** _______________\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"34b7e541-fc46-443f-9329-800f1caa525b","uuid":"6355e0a8-b677-4f3a-bac4-1e920685307e","timestamp":"2026-04-16T16:18:25.311Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\bev-diagnostic-rectification\\C05\\KK-01.md","content":"# KERTAS KERJA / WORK SHEET\n\n**Kod WIM / WIM Code:** G452-010-3:2023-C05/KK(1/4)\n**Kertas Warna / Paper Color:** BIRU / BLUE\n\n## Work Activity 1: Conduct BEV Daily Briefing\n\n## Objektif Prestasi\n1. Prepare daily briefing information and assignments\n2. Execute a daily briefing session\n3. Record daily briefing feedback and update the job control board\n\n## Materials\n- Briefing agenda template, attendance list form, job control board (whiteboard), sample work orders/job cards, marker pens\n\n## Prosedur Kerja\n\n### Step 1: Prepare Briefing\n1.1 Review previous day's job status on job control board\n1.2 Identify new vehicles received / scheduled for today\n1.3 Allocate tasks to technicians based on skill level and workload\n1.4 Prepare safety topic of the day\n1.5 Gather any service information updates (TSBs, recalls)\n1.6 Write briefing agenda\n\n### Step 2: Execute Briefing\n2.1 Gather all technicians at briefing area\n2.2 Circulate attendance list — all sign\n2.3 Deliver briefing following prepared agenda:\n   - Safety reminder (HV safety topic)\n   - Work progress update from yesterday\n   - New assignments — distribute job cards\n   - Service information updates\n   - Housekeeping / 5S compliance\n2.4 Invite questions and feedback\n2.5 Address concerns raised\n2.6 Close briefing — team disperses to assignments\n\n### Step 3: Post-Briefing Actions\n3.1 Update job control board with today's assignments\n3.2 File attendance list and briefing notes\n3.3 Document any safety concerns raised — initiate follow-up action\n3.4 Monitor work progress during the day\n\n## Assessment Checklist\n| Criteria | C | NYC |\n|----------|---|-----|\n| Briefing prepared with agenda covering all required items | [ ] | [ ] |\n| Briefing delivered clearly within 15-20 minutes | [ ] | [ ] |\n| Attendance list circulated and signed | [ ] | [ ] |\n| Job allocation matched to technician skill level | [ ] | [ ] |\n| Questions handled and feedback recorded | [ ] | [ ] |\n| Job control board updated | [ ] | [ ] |\n| Clear, confident communication demonstrated | [ ] | [ ] |\n\n**Trainee:** _______________ **Instructor:** _______________ **Date:** _______________\n","numLines":57,"startLine":1,"totalLines":57}}}
