{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QssAwkDZG7qLNLjMd4HCUS","type":"tool_result","content":"The file C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\bev-diagnostic-rectification\\C05\\KK-02.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"34b7e541-fc46-443f-9329-800f1caa525b","uuid":"5b6fdaad-2918-4126-a023-dddb33e8e740","timestamp":"2026-04-16T16:22:13.639Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\bev-diagnostic-rectification\\C05\\KK-02.md","oldString":"### Step 3: Identify Improvement Actions\n3.1 For areas rated below standard:\n   - Determine appropriate improvement technique (OJT, refresher, counselling, mentoring)\n   - If training needed: complete training nomination form\n   - If counselling needed: prepare counselling session agenda\n3.2 For top-performing areas: note recognition recommendations","newString":"### Step 3: Identify Improvement Actions\n3.1 For areas rated below standard:\n   - Determine appropriate improvement technique (OJT, refresher, counselling, mentoring)\n   - If training needed: complete training nomination form\n   - If counselling needed: prepare counselling session agenda\n3.2 For top-performing areas: note recognition recommendations\n3.3 For each improvement action, set a SMART target:\n   - Define the specific behaviour/skill to improve (Specific)\n   - State the measurable standard to be achieved (Measurable)\n   - Confirm the target is achievable with available resources (Achievable)\n   - Link the target directly to the technician's job role (Relevant)\n   - Set a review date (Time-bound)\n   - Document the SMART target in the counselling form","originalFile":"# KERTAS KERJA / WORK SHEET\n\n**Kod WIM / WIM Code:** G452-010-3:2023-C05/KK(2/4)\n**Kertas Warna / Paper Color:** BIRU / BLUE\n\n## Work Activity 2: Monitor BEV Subordinate's Performance\n\n## Objektif Prestasi\n1. Identify standard performance guidelines\n2. Evaluate subordinate performance using company evaluation form\n3. Identify improvement actions and complete a performance report\n\n## Materials\n- Performance evaluation form (company standard), counselling form, training nomination form, sample employee performance data\n\n## Prosedur Kerja\n\n### Step 1: Identify Performance Standards\n1.1 Review the company performance evaluation criteria\n1.2 Identify the evaluation dimensions: attitude, skills, knowledge, productivity\n1.3 Determine the BEV-specific competency indicators relevant to each subordinate\n\n### Step 2: Evaluate Performance\n2.1 Using the provided sample employee data, complete the evaluation form:\n   - Rate each dimension on the company scale\n   - Provide specific comments and examples for each rating\n   - Identify strengths and areas for improvement\n   - Calculate overall performance score\n\n### Step 3: Identify Improvement Actions\n3.1 For areas rated below standard:\n   - Determine appropriate improvement technique (OJT, refresher, counselling, mentoring)\n   - If training needed: complete training nomination form\n   - If counselling needed: prepare counselling session agenda\n3.2 For top-performing areas: note recognition recommendations\n\n### Step 4: Prepare Performance Report\n4.1 Compile evaluation results for all subordinates (sample data)\n4.2 Highlight top performers and those requiring intervention\n4.3 List recommendations with supporting evidence\n4.4 Prepare the report for submission to superior\n\n## Assessment Checklist\n| Criteria | C | NYC |\n|----------|---|-----|\n| Performance standards identified correctly | [ ] | [ ] |\n| Evaluation form completed accurately with specific comments | [ ] | [ ] |\n| Improvement actions appropriate to identified gaps | [ ] | [ ] |\n| Training nomination / counselling form completed where needed | [ ] | [ ] |\n| Performance report compiled and ready for superior | [ ] | [ ] |\n| Meticulous in evaluation, timely in completion | [ ] | [ ] |\n\n**Trainee:** _______________ **Instructor:** _______________ **Date:** _______________\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":33,"oldLines":6,"newStart":33,"newLines":13,"lines":["    - If training needed: complete training nomination form","    - If counselling needed: prepare counselling session agenda"," 3.2 For top-performing areas: note recognition recommendations","+3.3 For each improvement action, set a SMART target:","+   - Define the specific behaviour/skill to improve (Specific)","+   - State the measurable standard to be achieved (Measurable)","+   - Confirm the target is achievable with available resources (Achievable)","+   - Link the target directly to the technician's job role (Relevant)","+   - Set a review date (Time-bound)","+   - Document the SMART target in the counselling form"," "," ### Step 4: Prepare Performance Report"," 4.1 Compile evaluation results for all subordinates (sample data)"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01QKs4BzqekxHPbzea7YvhMb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Av1AiBeuEHNry6GHvv74Mf","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\bev-diagnostic-rectification\\C05\\KK-03.md","old_string":"### Step 4: Post-Training Documentation\n4.1 Describe the process for: collecting certificates, updating skills chart, evaluating effectiveness, sharing learnings","new_string":"### Step 4: Post-Training Documentation and Effectiveness Evaluation\n4.1 Collect training certificate/completion record and file in personnel record\n4.2 Update skills chart — mark the newly trained competency as \"Competent (Trained)\"\n4.3 Evaluate training effectiveness using Kirkpatrick levels:\n   - **Level 1 (Reaction):** Collect trainee's completed post-training feedback form\n   - **Level 2 (Learning):** Review post-training assessment results (test or practical)\n   - **Level 3 (Behaviour):** Observe technician performing the trained skill on the job after 30 days; document observation result\n4.4 Share key learnings from training during the next daily briefing"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":475,"cache_read_input_tokens":52438,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":475},"output_tokens":63,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"34b7e541-fc46-443f-9329-800f1caa525b","uuid":"57debbb2-3cc7-439f-b411-d75d7b481077"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Av1AiBeuEHNry6GHvv74Mf","type":"tool_result","content":"The file C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\bev-diagnostic-rectification\\C05\\KK-03.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"34b7e541-fc46-443f-9329-800f1caa525b","uuid":"87d90706-986d-47df-ac53-393c773c92d4","timestamp":"2026-04-16T16:22:23.102Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\bev-diagnostic-rectification\\C05\\KK-03.md","oldString":"### Step 4: Post-Training Documentation\n4.1 Describe the process for: collecting certificates, updating skills chart, evaluating effectiveness, sharing learnings","newString":"### Step 4: Post-Training Documentation and Effectiveness Evaluation\n4.1 Collect training certificate/completion record and file in personnel record\n4.2 Update skills chart — mark the newly trained competency as \"Competent (Trained)\"\n4.3 Evaluate training effectiveness using Kirkpatrick levels:\n   - **Level 1 (Reaction):** Collect trainee's completed post-training feedback form\n   - **Level 2 (Learning):** Review post-training assessment results (test or practical)\n   - **Level 3 (Behaviour):** Observe technician performing the trained skill on the job after 30 days; document observation result\n4.4 Share key learnings from training during the next daily briefing","originalFile":"# KERTAS KERJA / WORK SHEET\n\n**Kod WIM / WIM Code:** G452-010-3:2023-C05/KK(3/4)\n**Kertas Warna / Paper Color:** BIRU / BLUE\n\n## Work Activity 3: Coordinate BEV Subordinate's Training\n\n## Objektif Prestasi\n1. Identify training needs using a skills chart\n2. Perform Training Needs Analysis and complete TNA form\n3. Arrange subordinate training including logistics coordination\n\n## Materials\n- Skills chart template, TNA form, training plan template, sample training provider catalogue, training notification template\n\n## Prosedur Kerja\n\n### Step 1: Training Needs Identification (TNI)\n1.1 Review the skills chart for all subordinates\n1.2 Identify skill gaps — competencies marked as \"Not Competent\"\n1.3 Check for any new BEV service information requiring training\n1.4 Review recent performance evaluations for training recommendations\n1.5 List all identified training needs\n\n### Step 2: Training Needs Analysis (TNA)\n2.1 For each identified need, complete the TNA form:\n   - Current competency level\n   - Required competency level\n   - Gap severity (critical / important / desirable)\n   - Recommended training intervention type\n2.2 Create a skills matrix chart showing all technicians vs. competencies\n2.3 Prioritise training needs based on: safety impact, business impact, urgency\n\n### Step 3: Arrange Training\n3.1 Research available training programs (from sample catalogue):\n   - Training provider and accreditation\n   - Training location (in-house, external, online)\n   - Duration and schedule\n   - Cost\n3.2 Prepare annual training plan:\n   - Map each training need to a specific training program\n   - Schedule by quarter\n   - Assign budget\n3.3 Prepare training notification for selected technician(s)\n3.4 Arrange work coverage for training period\n\n### Step 4: Post-Training Documentation\n4.1 Describe the process for: collecting certificates, updating skills chart, evaluating effectiveness, sharing learnings\n\n## Assessment Checklist\n| Criteria | C | NYC |\n|----------|---|-----|\n| Skills chart reviewed and gaps identified | [ ] | [ ] |\n| TNA form completed with gap analysis | [ ] | [ ] |\n| Skills matrix chart created | [ ] | [ ] |\n| Training plan prepared with schedule and budget | [ ] | [ ] |\n| Training notification prepared | [ ] | [ ] |\n| Post-training documentation process described | [ ] | [ ] |\n| Resourceful in collecting training information | [ ] | [ ] |\n\n**Trainee:** _______________ **Instructor:** _______________ **Date:** _______________\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":44,"oldLines":8,"newStart":44,"newLines":14,"lines":[" 3.3 Prepare training notification for selected technician(s)"," 3.4 Arrange work coverage for training period"," ","-### Step 4: Post-Training Documentation","-4.1 Describe the process for: collecting certificates, updating skills chart, evaluating effectiveness, sharing learnings","+### Step 4: Post-Training Documentation and Effectiveness Evaluation","+4.1 Collect training certificate/completion record and file in personnel record","+4.2 Update skills chart — mark the newly trained competency as \"Competent (Trained)\"","+4.3 Evaluate training effectiveness using Kirkpatrick levels:","+   - **Level 1 (Reaction):** Collect trainee's completed post-training feedback form","+   - **Level 2 (Learning):** Review post-training assessment results (test or practical)","+   - **Level 3 (Behaviour):** Observe technician performing the trained skill on the job after 30 days; document observation result","+4.4 Share key learnings from training during the next daily briefing"," "," ## Assessment Checklist"," | Criteria | C | NYC |"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_015o5NA5xZB5v1KxCBqqd93H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NysagDm4tcmxZYYFwxo8fC","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\bev-diagnostic-rectification\\C05\\KK-04.md","old_string":"### Step 1: Interpret SHE Checklist\n1.1 Obtain the company SHE checklist\n1.2 Review all checklist items — understand what each item requires\n1.3 Identify BEV-specific items: HV signage, insulated mats, rescue hooks, fire extinguishers (Class D), PPE condition, waste management","new_string":"### Step 1: Interpret SHE Checklist\n1.1 Obtain the company SHE checklist\n1.2 Review all checklist items — understand what each item requires\n1.3 Identify BEV-specific items: HV signage, insulated mats, rescue hooks, fire extinguishers (Class D), PPE condition, waste management\n1.4 Check the Chemical Register and verify Safety Data Sheets (SDS) are accessible at each point of chemical use (coolants, refrigerants, solvents)\n1.5 Verify the emergency contact list is displayed and all numbers are current"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":407,"cache_read_input_tokens":52913,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":407},"output_tokens":63,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"34b7e541-fc46-443f-9329-800f1caa525b","uuid":"4fa0ae87-a725-4f29-8da7-26302d83af92"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NysagDm4tcmxZYYFwxo8fC","type":"tool_result","content":"The file C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\bev-diagnostic-rectification\\C05\\KK-04.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"34b7e541-fc46-443f-9329-800f1caa525b","uuid":"d931b154-0b07-4f43-8e9b-38879bd739dd","timestamp":"2026-04-16T16:22:32.562Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\bev-diagnostic-rectification\\C05\\KK-04.md","oldString":"### Step 1: Interpret SHE Checklist\n1.1 Obtain the company SHE checklist\n1.2 Review all checklist items — understand what each item requires\n1.3 Identify BEV-specific items: HV signage, insulated mats, rescue hooks, fire extinguishers (Class D), PPE condition, waste management","newString":"### Step 1: Interpret SHE Checklist\n1.1 Obtain the company SHE checklist\n1.2 Review all checklist items — understand what each item requires\n1.3 Identify BEV-specific items: HV signage, insulated mats, rescue hooks, fire extinguishers (Class D), PPE condition, waste management\n1.4 Check the Chemical Register and verify Safety Data Sheets (SDS) are accessible at each point of chemical use (coolants, refrigerants, solvents)\n1.5 Verify the emergency contact list is displayed and all numbers are current","originalFile":"# KERTAS KERJA / WORK SHEET\n\n**Kod WIM / WIM Code:** G452-010-3:2023-C05/KK(4/4)\n**Kertas Warna / Paper Color:** BIRU / BLUE\n\n## Work Activity 4: Monitor BEV Workshop Safety, Health & Environment\n\n## Objektif Prestasi\n1. Interpret and complete a workshop SHE checklist\n2. Conduct a workshop SHE walk-through inspection\n3. Prepare a SHE finding report with risk assessment and recommendations\n\n## Materials\n- SHE checklist (company standard), SHE finding report template, risk assessment matrix, camera (for photo documentation), clipboard and pen\n\n## Prosedur Kerja\n\n### Step 1: Interpret SHE Checklist\n1.1 Obtain the company SHE checklist\n1.2 Review all checklist items — understand what each item requires\n1.3 Identify BEV-specific items: HV signage, insulated mats, rescue hooks, fire extinguishers (Class D), PPE condition, waste management\n\n### Step 2: Conduct SHE Walk-Through\n2.1 Walk through the workshop systematically (bay by bay)\n2.2 For each area, check every item on the SHE checklist:\n\n**Safety items to check:**\n- HV warning signage in place at all BEV bays\n- Barrier stanchions available and in good condition\n- Insulated mats present at HV work positions\n- Electric rescue hooks accessible at each bay\n- Fire extinguishers (Class D): in place, serviced, pressure OK\n- First aid kits stocked\n- Emergency exits clear and marked\n- PPE storage area organised, all PPE serviceable\n- Insulated tools stored properly, inspected recently\n\n**Health items:**\n- Ventilation adequate\n- Lighting sufficient (500 lux at work surface)\n- Ergonomic concerns (lifting equipment available)\n- Noise levels acceptable\n- AED accessible\n\n**Environment items:**\n- Waste containers properly labeled and segregated\n- Secondary containment in place for liquid waste\n- Waste inventory log up to date\n- No spills or contamination on floor\n- Scheduled waste storage area compliant\n\n2.3 Take photos of any findings (positive or negative)\n2.4 Record findings on the SHE checklist\n\n### Step 3: Prepare SHE Finding Report\n3.1 For each non-compliant finding:\n   - Describe the finding\n   - Attach photo evidence\n   - Assess risk (severity x likelihood = risk rating)\n   - Provide recommendation for corrective action\n   - Assign responsible person\n   - Set target completion date\n\n3.2 For positive findings:\n   - Note good practices observed\n   - Recognise individuals or teams\n\n### Step 4: Report Submission\n4.1 Compile all findings into the SHE report\n4.2 Prioritise: critical/high-risk findings first\n4.3 Submit report to superior\n4.4 Follow up on corrective actions by target dates\n\n## Assessment Checklist\n| Criteria | C | NYC |\n|----------|---|-----|\n| SHE checklist correctly interpreted | [ ] | [ ] |\n| Systematic walk-through conducted | [ ] | [ ] |\n| BEV-specific safety items checked | [ ] | [ ] |\n| Photo documentation taken for findings | [ ] | [ ] |\n| Risk assessment completed for each finding | [ ] | [ ] |\n| Recommendations are practical and specific | [ ] | [ ] |\n| Report compiled and ready for submission | [ ] | [ ] |\n| Attentive to details throughout inspection | [ ] | [ ] |\n\n**Trainee:** _______________ **Instructor:** _______________ **Date:** _______________\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":19,"oldLines":6,"newStart":19,"newLines":8,"lines":[" 1.1 Obtain the company SHE checklist"," 1.2 Review all checklist items — understand what each item requires"," 1.3 Identify BEV-specific items: HV signage, insulated mats, rescue hooks, fire extinguishers (Class D), PPE condition, waste management","+1.4 Check the Chemical Register and verify Safety Data Sheets (SDS) are accessible at each point of chemical use (coolants, refrigerants, solvents)","+1.5 Verify the emergency contact list is displayed and all numbers are current"," "," ### Step 2: Conduct SHE Walk-Through"," 2.1 Walk through the workshop systematically (bay by bay)"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
